            <div xml:id="d667">

                <pb facs="0922" n="910" sameAs="frus:frus1945v06/pg910"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 PW/8–1645: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-08-16T17:00:00+01:00">August 16, 1945—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 16—3:41 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>8299. Refer despatch 145 dated June 23.<anchor n="5" xml:id="d667-f1"/> From
                    Hodgson. War Crimes Commission adopted Commission document C. 122 at meeting of
                    Aug 15. Chinese representative informed Commission that Chungking Subcommission
                    approved the document. [Hodgson.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
